docs/specs/workspace.json: {"id":"WS-ID-01","criterion":"A package whose name is claimed by no other directory gets a bare id equal to its manifest name (for example `foo` or `@scope/foo`)."}
docs/specs/workspace.json: {"id":"WS-ID-02","criterion":"A dual-manifest package (one directory with several admitted manifests) is one package whose id comes from Cargo.toml, else package.json, else pyproject.toml, and each manifest's own name still resolves to that package within its ecosystem -- including through `--package`, `add` and a changeset entry naming the package by a non-primary manifest's own name, not only its primary name."}
docs/specs/workspace.json: {"id":"WS-ID-03","criterion":"When two or more directories declare the same name and no ecosystem declares it in more than one of them, each package is promoted to an ecosystem-qualified id, displayed as `cargo/foo`. Promotion preserves the package's key (its workspace-relative directory) and CHANGELOG path; `cargo/foo` selects it in both states. Newly created default tags use `{display id}@{version}`, so promotion changes their namespace. A promoted package's last tag is also found among `foo@*` tags whose commit contains its manifest and no other same-named package's. A bare `pre.json` `initialVersions` key moves to the one same-named package that existed when `pre.json` was added, else `version` fails with E245."}
docs/specs/workspace.json: {"id":"WS-ID-05","criterion":"A `[[fixed-group]]` or `[[linked-group]]` member written `cargo:foo` or `cargo/foo` resolves to package `foo` when a Cargo manifest declares `foo`, promoted or not, through the same selector resolver used for `--package` and changesets; a member naming an ecosystem with no such manifest fails loading with E108, and a bare member name ambiguous across ecosystems fails loading with E103 (not E108).","is_error_case":true}
docs/specs/workspace.json: {"id":"WS-ID-06","criterion":"A changeset, `callisto add --package` or `callisto matrix --package` naming the bare name of promoted packages fails with E103 listing every qualified candidate and showing the qualified form to write; naming a package that does not exist under that name in that ecosystem fails with E102.","is_error_case":true}
docs/specs/workspace.json: {"id":"WS-ID-09","criterion":"A discovered package whose canonical manifests use different version grammars fails with E007 before version planning or init writes. This includes co-located Cargo.toml and pyproject.toml, whether the Python version is static or declared dynamic; matching numeric version strings do not bypass the grammar check.","is_error_case":true}
docs/specs/workspace.json: {"id":"WS-CFG-01","criterion":"For each package, the first ecosystem-prefixed `[[package]]` rule whose ecosystem the package actually has a manifest in and whose name matches applies, regardless of declaration order relative to bare rules; a prefixed rule for an ecosystem the package has no manifest in never applies, even to a same-named package in another ecosystem. If no prefixed rule applies, the first matching bare rule applies."}
docs/specs/cli.json: {"id":"CLI-OUT-05","criterion":"With `--format json`, the status, add, init, pre and snapshot reports on stdout are single JSON objects with camelCase keys and a top-level `schemaVersion`, `command` (the subcommand name) and `dryRun`."}
docs/specs/cli.json: {"id":"CLI-ADD-01","criterion":"`callisto add --package <name>:<severity> --summary <text>` (--package repeatable, bare or qualified names such as `cargo/app`, severity none, patch, minor or major) writes `.changeset/<adjective>-<noun>-<verb>.md` with front matter mapping each package to its severity and the trimmed summary as body, prints `Added changeset: <path>`, and never prompts."}
docs/specs/cli.json: {"id":"CLI-INIT-01","criterion":"Before any question, `callisto init` prints `Detected:` with the ecosystems, the origin remote URL, and each package's qualified id, version, last tag, and binary names for binary-producing packages."}
docs/specs/cli.json: {"id":"CLI-INIT-02","criterion":"Interactive init asks only: versioning (independent or fixed); whether to ship binaries as GitHub release assets, only when a package produces a binary; the product package, only when more than one does; the forge repository, pre-filled from origin; comma-separated target triples; whether to generate a workflow (default no); and whether to write callisto.toml (default yes)."}
docs/specs/cli.json: {"id":"CLI-INIT-12","criterion":"init exits 1 without writing for an empty or repeated target triple, --artifact-target when no package produces a binary, a --product-package that is absent or not binary-producing, a --forge-repository that is not `owner/repo` or differs from origin's GitHub repository, or --forge-repository or --product-package given without --artifact-target.","is_error_case":true}
docs/specs/cli.json: {"id":"CLI-WF-03","criterion":"Without artifact slots or platform packages, the generated workflow triggers on push to the detected default branch (local `origin/HEAD`, else a live query of `origin`, else the checked-out branch, else `main`) and has two jobs: `version-pr` running callisto-action with `mode: version-pr` and that same `branch`, and `release` running it with `mode: release` and a token secret per detected ecosystem (CARGO_REGISTRY_TOKEN, NPM_TOKEN with NPM_CONFIG_PROVENANCE, PYPI_TOKEN) plus GH_TOKEN. init's human-readable output names which of those sources resolved the branch."}
docs/specs/cli.json: {"id":"CLI-WF-04","criterion":"When binaries ship as artifact slots or the workspace has napi platform packages, the generated workflow has `version-pr`, `plan` (runs `callisto release plan --from-release-commit` when the pushed commit adds or modifies .callisto/release-decision.json), `build` (a matrix from napi targets and artifact slots), and `execute` (runs `callisto release artifact-manifest` and `callisto release execute`) jobs."}
docs/specs/cli.json: {"id":"CLI-WF-06","criterion":"For a workspace with maturin platform targets, or platform packages without napi targets, init prints `Skipping GitHub Actions workflow generation: <reason>.`, records a warning diagnostic in the JSON report, and exits 1 instead when --workflow was given.","is_error_case":true}
docs/specs/cli.json: {"id":"CLI-SCHEMA-01","criterion":"`callisto schema` prints the StatusReport JSON Schema; `--type` is a fixed value enum selecting another report type, and an unrecognized value is a clap usage error (exit 2) listing the supported values."}
docs/specs/release.json: {"id":"REL-CMD-01","criterion":"`callisto release` selects every package that has a publish target other than `none` and whose current version has no matching tag. For each one it runs the registry publishes, creates the git tag, and creates the GitHub release when `github-release` is a target."}
